🎮 3-Lane Rail Shooter (Browser Prototype)

Let’s design a clean, simple version you could build fast.

🧱 Core Game Structure (Browser Canvas)
1️⃣ Layout

Visually it would look like:

| Lane 1 | Lane 2 | Lane 3 |
Enemies move downward toward player
Player fixed at bottom

You don’t move forward — enemies move toward you.




2️⃣ Core Mechanics
🎯 Player

Fixed at bottom center

Can:

Shoot (auto or click)

Switch lanes (← → keys)

👾 Enemies

Spawn at top

Move downward

Disappear when shot

Cause damage if they reach bottom

🎁 Power-Ups

Spawn randomly inside waves:

🔫 Better gun (faster fire)

❤️ Extra life

💣 Bomb

🛡 Shield

🏗 Basic Architecture (Simple & Clean)

Since you’re already using <canvas>, this structure works well:

Game
 ├── Player
 ├── Bullets[]
 ├── Enemies[]
 ├── PowerUps[]
 ├── WaveManager
 └── InputHandler
🌀 Wave System (Important Part)

Each wave could be an array of lane spawns:

[
  { lane: 0, type: "enemy" },
  { lane: 1, type: "enemy" },
  { lane: 2, type: "powerup" }
]

Spawn waves every X seconds.

Difficulty increases by:

Faster enemy speed

More enemies per wave

Fewer powerups

Tougher enemy types

🔁 Game Loop (Core Engine)
function gameLoop() {
    update();
    draw();
    requestAnimationFrame(gameLoop);
}

Inside update():

Move enemies

Move bullets

Check collisions

Remove destroyed objects

🎨 Visually Simple First Version

Start with:

Rectangles for enemies

Circles for bullets

Different colors for powerups

You don’t need graphics at first.

⚙ Minimal Prototype Plan (Build in 1–2 Hours)

Phase 1:

3 lanes

Enemies falling

Click to shoot

Basic collision detection

Phase 2:

Lane switching

Wave system

Score counter

Phase 3:

Powerups

Sound

Difficulty scaling

🧠 Important Design Decision
Do you want:

A) Player locked to one lane at a time
B) Player shoots freely across all lanes
C) Auto-shooter (no aiming)

For a fast prototype, I recommend:

🔥 Player locked to a lane + auto fire

It’s simple and feels good quickly.

